32
00:04:11,553 --> 00:04:18,958
[SPEAKER_01]: So, like, it kind of depends why you're doing it and what you can sort of discern are the correct reasons.

33
00:04:19,018 --> 00:04:30,267
[SPEAKER_01]: And in this case, that monk, obviously, you know, you can kind of lean a bit towards the side of more asceticism, because that will be, you know,

34
00:04:30,691 --> 00:04:40,215
[SPEAKER_01]: Still a bit safer than leaning towards the side of just letting yourself do whatever you want, but at the same time you have to be discerning that middle ground, which is the Middle Way.

35
00:04:40,755 --> 00:04:45,517
[SPEAKER_01]: And that comes down again to basically under starting to understand the Four Noble Truths.

36
00:04:45,617 --> 00:04:55,481
[SPEAKER_01]: So, aligning yourselves with those Four Noble Truths, the Middle Way being the the path or the way to actually free yourself from suffering through

37
00:05:01,906 --> 00:05:08,872
